  "visual_observations": [
    "High plateaus are approximately 1.4-1.6 vertical divisions above low across the three conditions, about 7-8 V assuming physical probe attenuation matches the X10 menu",
    "Rising-edge overshoot remains plainly visible with the GT physically absent at both 20 us/div and 100 us/div",
    "Rounded falling tails and return near the displayed reference level persist with the GT absent",
    "No obvious gross amplitude collapse, clipping or persistent level shift is visible between unplugged, attached/OFF and attached/LISTEN windows"
  ],
  "visual_derivation": "The mere presence of the peaks and rounded tails cannot be attributed to GT LISTEN, because they also occur with the GT physically absent. A smaller GT contribution is not excluded.",
  "bounded_conclusion": "No observed read-data or retry degradation and no obvious gross waveform deterioration in these isolated-bench E54 high-speed read comparisons",
  "limitations": [
    "Different packets and bit patterns were photographed; pulse-width differences are not evidence of loading changes",
    "Camera perspective, focus, exposure and scope rendering prevent reliable small voltage, overshoot or edge-time deltas",
    "Probe compensation, calibration and physical attenuation were not independently verified",
    "Short displayed windows cannot exclude rare disturbances or unintended pulses outside those windows",
    "Shared bus voltage does not establish which device drove a particular pulse",
    "Single matched condition runs do not establish statistically significant timing changes",
    "Read-only tests do not qualify AL5 programming, recovery or monitoring during a flash",
    "Fixed 4x monitoring does not establish continuity across 1x/4x transitions.",
    "HTX comparison is relative to the decoded application trace, whose physical-bus completeness is unknown.",
    "The photos are original camera images of the scope screen, not raw waveform sample records.",
    "This experiment does not qualify MultiMap selector/latch logic, RAM ownership, interrupt/fault behavior, or engine operation.",
    "Private trace inputs are identified by hashes but are not included, so the full packet comparison cannot be reproduced from this publication alone."
  ],
